kit_relocate.py script b3f6713fe96aff2c0a508238be941648ae604031a26d353e9f60d787e83ab773 the script of record: copies libreac/fuzz_decode's released plain / UBSan lib (K1), moves every image value to this unit's binaries (K2), adds second-donor libc walks when linked (K3); its docstring states each step and control. It is the shared libdiginet kit relocation script as run for the tables here (sha256 967abd6019c3) with three changes: its docstrings name no internal path and no longer name a summary file it never wrote; the roadapt path it rewords in donor comments is written as two adjacent string literals, which Python joins into the same constant; and the evidence path its notices name is kit-relocation/values.tsv (this directory and table were renamed from k2/k2-values.tsv, and the 159 notices in lib/ that cite it were changed the same way). Against the first script of record (sha256 6335e2012e0c) it adds rule (g) and names decode's two harness check functions (check_round_trip, check_braid) as harness files that are never kept; against 8f17a31858b9 it dates every notice it writes from --month (YYYY-MM, no day, no agent, one notice on each file whose text differs from the donor's) and adds rule (h). Step (d'): a YH03 data cell that no donor symbol covers moves by content, when the donor bytes from the cell to the next donor symbol (8 to 64 bytes) occur exactly once in this unit's loaded image. On this unit it moved one cell, plain src0_D_debruijn32: 0x10480 -> 0x10460. The ubsan cell moved by the existing rule (0x10488 -> 0x10500), which equals the unique content match. Step (g): a decimal address inside a driver string constant (YL0v's rodata_*_src1 lemmas and the YL0w / YL0x / YL0y walks that read them) moves with its whole NUL-terminated string, which must occur once in this unit's image. On this unit it moved 66365 -> 66389 ("cli: cannot open %s\n" + 19) and 66388 -> 66412 ("cli: read error on %s\n" + 21) in Reusable/YL0v.v, YL0w.v, YL0w_cfw.v and their U/ twin